{"The new advanced pagination path allows negative offsets and passes them directly to Django QuerySet slicing (queryset[start_offset:stop] where start_offset < 0), but Django does not support negative indexing and raises AssertionError, causing 500 errors for any request with a negative cursor offset": 0.9437920451164246, "Switching span buffers from Redis sets to sorted sets (zcard, zunionstore, zpopmin) assumes existing span-buf:s:* keys are already sorted sets, but in production they are plain sets written via SADD, causing Redis WRONGTYPE errors that abort the Lua script and drop spans for up to an hour": 0.951889157295227, "Switching span buckets from Redis sets to sorted sets issues ZADD against keys that already exist as SETs in production, causing WRONGTYPE errors since Redis refuses to change a key's type, breaking span ingestion for up to redis_ttl (3600s) after deploy": 0.9740427136421204}